{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>It smoked.</b> This עָשַׁן is not a noun, for the shin has a patach — but it is a verb, like אָמַר, שָׁמַר, שָׁמַע. Therefore its Targum is תְּנַן כֻּלֵּהּ, and he did not render תְּנָנָא. And every עָשָׁן in Scripture has a kamatz vowel, because they are nouns." "<b>Like a furnace.</b> Of lime. One might think like this furnace and no more — therefore Scripture says ״בּוֹעֵר בָּאֵשׁ עַד לֵב הַשָּׁמַיִם״ (Deuteronomy 4). And what does Scripture mean by ״like a furnace״? To give the ear something it is capable of hearing — He gives creatures a recognizable sign. So too ״כְּאַרְיֵה יִשְׁאָג״ (Hosea 11) — and who gave the lion its strength but He? Yet Scripture likens Him to a lion. Rather, we describe and compare Him to His creatures in order to give the ear something it can hear. So too ״וְקוֹלוֹ כְּקוֹל מַיִם רַבִּים״ (Ezekiel 43) — and who gave the waters a voice but He? Yet you describe Him, comparing Him to His creatures — in order to give the ear something it can hear (Mekhilta)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:53:13.235115079Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}